a major Republican donor in Florida is  threatening to cut off funding to  politicians who oppose a ban on assault  weapons al Hoffman jr. has raised  hundreds of millions of dollars for  Republicans but in the wake of the  shooting at Stoneman Douglas High School  Hoffman sent an email to other GOP  donors urging them to support a ban on  assault weapons  Jericka Duncan sat down with Hoffman at  his Florida home she's in parkland  Jericka good morning good morning the  longtime GOP fundraiser and wealthy real  estate developer said he literally  helped build this community but after  last week's deadly shooting he now says  that his influence and dollars will be  determined by one major issue when you  first heard about that shooting at a  school another school shooting what was  your initial reaction I was incredulous  I couldn't believe it I thought I had my  heart in my hands that feeling led 83  year old Republican donor al Hoffman jr.  to stop contributing to his own party's  candidates unless they support a change  in the gun laws I will not write a check  for anyone who does not propose a ban on  assault weapons you were quoted as  saying this particular shooting was the  end of the road for you that's right why  not a Sandy Hook well I've been after so  many politicians to adopt legislation  and always the answer is that well we're  working on it we're working on and  nothing ever changes the original  federal assault weapons ban was passed  in September of 1994 but expired after  ten years between May 2003 and June 2008  there were at least 17 attempts to renew  or replace the ban but none made it to a  vote and an effort to pass a permanent  ban after the 2012 Sandy Hook massacre  failed to get Senate approval last  Friday Hoffman wrote an email to half  dozen GOP donors asking them to follow  his lead would you be willing to write a  check to Democrats and Republicans who  are in favor of the ban I would support  a fiscally conservative person who  supports the ban and at this moment in  time I really don't care whether it's a  republic  Democrat do you really believe something  will change as a result of the parkland  shooting don't know I hope so  where's just a start right now but I  think we need to build the movement and  time and the Lord willing we'll be will  accomplish some things Hoffman also said  that he sent an email to Florida  Governor Rick Scott who's considering a  Senate run we reached out to Scott for  comment and have not heard back yet gale  all right there we go we all hope  something will change thank you very  much
 

